{"id":"imagebuilder","corpus":"aws","title":"EC2 Image Builder","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/what-is-image-builder.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"EC2 Image Builder"},{"kind":"p","text":"EC2 Image Builder is a fully managed AWS service that helps you to automate the creation, management, and deployment of customized, secure, and up-to-date server images. You can use the AWS Management Console, AWS Command Line Interface, or APIs to create custom images in your AWS account."},{"kind":"p","text":"You own the customized images that Image Builder creates in your account. You can configure pipelines to automate updates and system patching for the images that you own. You can also run a stand-alone command to create an image with the configuration resources that you've defined."},{"kind":"p","text":"The Image Builder pipeline wizard can guide you through the steps to create a custom image, as follows:"},{"kind":"li","text":"Name your pipeline and add tags."},{"kind":"li","text":"Define metadata and vulnerability scan settings."},{"kind":"li","text":"Set up a schedule for your pipeline."},{"kind":"p","text":"You can select an existing recipe or create a new one."},{"kind":"li","text":"Choose a base image for your customizations."},{"kind":"li","text":"Add to or remove software from your base image."},{"kind":"li","text":"Customize settings and scripts with build components."},{"kind":"li","text":"Select test components to run."},{"kind":"p","text":"An image workflow defines the sequence of steps that Image Builder performs during the build and test stages of the image creation process. This is part of the overall Image Builder workflow framework."},{"kind":"li","text":"Select an IAM role to associate with the instance profile for instances that Image Builder launches during the image creation process."},{"kind":"li","text":"Select one or more instance types that can be applied at launch."},{"kind":"li","text":"Select an Amazon Simple Notification Service (SNS) Topic to receive notifications from Image Builder."},{"kind":"li","text":"Specify VPC, subnet, and security groups that apply for the image creation process."},{"kind":"li","text":"Select troubleshooting settings such as where Image Builder writes logs, and whether to terminate the build instance on failure (default) or keep it running for further troubleshooting."},{"kind":"li","text":"Select AWS Regions where Image Builder distributes your Amazon Machine Image (AMI) or container image."},{"kind":"li","text":"If your Image Builder pipeline creates an AMI, Image Builder also supports the following configuration:"},{"kind":"li","text":"Select a KMS key to use for encryption."},{"kind":"li","text":"Configure AMI sharing across AWS accounts and Organizations."},{"kind":"li","text":"Associate a License Manager self-managed license with your distributed image."},{"kind":"li","text":"Configure a launch template for your image."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Features of Image Builder"},{"kind":"p","text":"EC2 Image Builder provides the following features:"},{"kind":"p","text":"Increase productivity and reduce operations for building compliant and up-to-date images"},{"kind":"p","text":"Image Builder reduces the amount of work involved in creating and managing images at scale by automating your build pipelines. You can automate your builds by providing your build execution schedule preference. Automation reduces the operational cost of maintaining your software with the latest operating system patches."},{"kind":"p","text":"Increase service uptime"},{"kind":"p","text":"Image Builder provides access to test components that you can use to test your images before deployment. You can also create custom test components with AWS Task Orchestrator and Executor (AWSTOE), and use those. Image Builder distributes your image only if all of the configured tests have succeeded."},{"kind":"p","text":"Raise the security bar for deployments"},{"kind":"p","text":"Image Builder allows you to create images that remove unnecessary exposure to component security vulnerabilities. You can apply AWS security settings to create secure, out-of-the-box images that meet industry and internal security criteria. Image Builder also provides collections of settings for companies in regulated industries. You can use these settings to help you quickly and easily build compliant images for STIG standards. For a complete list of STIG components available through Image Builder, see Amazon managed STIG hardening components for Image Builder."},{"kind":"p","text":"Centralized enforcement and lineage tracking"},{"kind":"p","text":"Using built-in integrations with AWS Organizations, Image Builder enables you to enforce policies that restrict accounts to run instances only from approved AMIs."},{"kind":"p","text":"Simplified sharing of resources across AWS accounts"},{"kind":"p","text":"EC2 Image Builder integrates with AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to allow you to share certain resources with any AWS account or through AWS Organizations. EC2 Image Builder resources that can be shared are:"},{"kind":"li","text":"Components"},{"kind":"li","text":"Images"},{"kind":"li","text":"Image recipes"},{"kind":"li","text":"Container recipes"},{"kind":"p","text":"For more information, see Share Image Builder resources with AWS RAM."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Supported operating systems"},{"kind":"p","text":"Image Builder supports the following operating system versions:"},{"kind":"h2","text":"Supported image formats"},{"kind":"p","text":"For your custom images that create an Amazon Machine Image (AMI), you can choose an existing AMI as a starting point. For Docker container images, you can choose from public images hosted on DockerHub, existing container images in Amazon ECR, or Amazon-managed container images as your starting point."}],"lemmas":{"imaged":["imaged","image"],"imaging":["imaging","image"],"builders":["builder","builders"],"fullies":["fullies","fully"],"managed":["managed","manage"],"manageds":["manageds","managed"],"manages":["manages","manage"],"services":["service","services"],"serviced":["serviced","service"],"servicing":["servicing","service"],"helps":["help","helps"],"helping":["helping","help"],"helped":["helped","help"],"automates":["automates","automate"],"creations":["creation","creations"],"managements":["management","managements"],"customized":["customized","customize"],"customizeds":["customizeds","customized"],"customizes":["customizes","customize"],"secures":["secures","secure"],"secured":["secured","secure"],"securing":["securing","secure"],"dates":["date","dates"],"dated":["dated","date"],"dating":["dating","date"],"servers":["server","servers"],"images":["image","images"],"uses":["use","uses"],"used":["used","use"],"consoles":["console","consoles"],"commands":["command","commands"],"commanded":["commanded","command"],"commanding":["commanding","command"],"lines":["line","lines"],"lining":["lining","line"],"lined":["lined","line"],"interfaces":["interface","interfaces"],"apis":["apis","api"],"created":["created","create"],"customs":["custom","customs"],"accounting":["accounting","account"],"accounted":["accounted","account"],"owns":["owns","own"],"owned":["owned","own"],"owning":["owning","own"],"creates":["creates","create"],"configures":["configures","configure"],"pipelines":["pipeline","pipelines"],"updates":["update","updates"],"updating":["updating","update"],"updated":["updated","update"],"patching":["patching","patch"],"patchings":["patching","patchings"],"patched":["patched","patch"],"runs":["run","runs"],"ran":["ran","run"],"stands":["stand","stands"],"standing":["standing","stand"],"stood":["stood","stand"],"alones":["alones","alone"],"configurations":["configuration","configurations"],"resources":["resource","resources"],"you'ves":["you'ves","you've"],"defined":["defined","define"],"defineds":["defineds","defined"],"defi